From a55da3e4236bbb7103936f26277b3867b9646ea9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:48:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Building close-out cleanup: dead text and half-wired tiers
 (audit 2026-09-29)

- Dissolution Chamber T3: per-tier deltas, so slotting costs 10 and
  disenchant pays +10 as the text says (were 0 and +15).
- Arcane Library T1: the browser claim removed (it opens without the
  building); T1 now gives the first Insight card.
- Undercroft T1: without the building the guild runs 1 informant, so T1's
  2 is a real step.
- Overrun buildings stop working for the council and the table too:
  CouncilQueries.BuildingTier, the parley opening hand and the building
  cards read the working tier.
- Grand Hall short of seats (blighted): the latest charters past the seat
  count go dark, and the charter lists say so.
- Scribe's Tower T2: a party whose dive ends at a staging anchor or the
  parked castle recharges its wands there.
- Text: Chancery, Undercroft, Scrying (objective only when the run has
  one; no patrol charting), Scriptorum (halves, not branches;
  Dissemination's +3 points), spellglass, teleport refusal; stale
  comments in TeleportSigil and CycleState.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RF7HNp6pvyXiAz229q52Px
